1
00:00:00,102 --> 00:00:01,562
I did your horoscope, remember?

2
00:00:01,729 --> 00:00:05,229
I was gonna do everybody's until Sheldon
went on one of his psychotic rants.

3
00:00:06,025 --> 00:00:07,905
(Sheldon:)For the record, that psychotic rant...

4
00:00:08,069 --> 00:00:10,949
(Sheldon:)...was a concise summation
of the research of Bertram Forer...

5
00:00:11,113 --> 00:00:13,493
(Sheldon:)...who, in 1948, proved conclusively...

6
00:00:13,657 --> 00:00:15,497
...through meticulous experiments...

7
00:00:15,659 --> 00:00:17,999
(Sheldon:)...that astrology
is pseudoscientific hokum.

8
00:00:18,162 --> 00:00:19,992
Blah, blah, blah. Typical Taurus.

9
00:00:21,457 --> 00:00:24,087
- So we gonna see you Saturday?
- I don't think so.

10
00:00:24,251 --> 00:00:26,171
(Penny:)- Why not?
- I don't celebrate my birthday.

11
00:00:26,337 --> 00:00:27,507
Shut up. Yeah, you do.

12
00:00:27,671 --> 00:00:29,841
(Leonard:)It's no big deal.
It's the way I was raised.

13
00:00:30,007 --> 00:00:32,467
My parents focused
on celebrating achievements...

14
00:00:32,635 --> 00:00:36,385
(Leonard:)...and being expelled from a birth canal
was not considered one of them.

15
00:00:36,889 --> 00:00:40,059
(Penny:)- That's so silly.
- It's actually based on very sound theories.

16
00:00:40,226 --> 00:00:43,146
(Sheldon:)- His mother published a paper on it.
- Well, what was it called?

17
00:00:43,312 --> 00:00:45,692
"I Hate My Son
and That's Why He Can't Have Cake"?

18
00:00:46,816 --> 00:00:48,446
SHELDON:
It was obviously effective.

19
00:00:48,609 --> 00:00:50,819
(Sheldon:)Leonard grew up to be
an experimental physicist.

20
00:00:50,986 --> 00:00:54,696
(Sheldon:)Perhaps if she'd also denied him Christmas,
he'd be a little better at it.

21
00:00:55,533 --> 00:00:57,363
(Leonard:)Thank you.

22
00:00:57,535 --> 00:01:01,375
(Howard:)Well, I love birthdays. Waking up
to Mom's special French-toast breakfast...

